    <VI_Package_Configuration_File>VI Helpeks (LV2014).vipc</VI_Package_Configuration_File>
    <Description>
      <One_Line_Description_Summary>Utility to create HTML/CHM help for LabVIEW VIs and Palettes</One_Line_Description_Summary>
      <Description>VI Helpeks is a toolkit providing UI tools and API VIs for building professional HTML/CHM help for VIs and Function Palettes. It automatically generates documentation in the native LabVIEW Help style by collecting information directly from the source VIs, while offering extensive options to customize the final output.

-- Launch the VI Helpeks UI using the "Tools &gt;&gt; VI Helpeks" menu. This is a manager for VI Helpeks projects used to create VI documentation.
-- You can open and safely build example projects in the VI Helpeks UI using its "Help &gt;&gt; Examples" menu.
-- API VIs can be found in the "Addons &gt;&gt; VI Helpeks API" functions palette. Examples of the API VIs usage can be opened using the "Tools &gt;&gt; VI Helpeks" menu. You can also launch the NI Example Finder and search for "VIHelpeks", or  find it in the "&lt;labview&gt;\Examples\VI Helpeks" folder.
-- When launched from a specific VI's "Tools &gt;&gt; VI Helpeks" menu, the "VI Documentation" utility opens to help you review and edit documentation properties of that specific VI and its controls.
</Description>
      <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2012-2026 Konstantin Shifershteyn</Copyright>
      <Packager>Konstantin Shifershteyn</Packager>
      <URL>https://github.com/konstantin-shifershteyn/vihelpeks</URL>
      <Release_Notes>&lt;b&gt;VI Helpeks 3.1.0&lt;/b&gt;
-- VI Helpeks has transitioned to &lt;b&gt;Open Source&lt;/b&gt; project under the terms on the &lt;b&gt;MIT License&lt;/b&gt;. All source code of the Toolkit is available at GitHub:
https://github.com/konstantin-shifershteyn/vihelpeks
-- UI code updated to improve usability and fix bugs.
-- HTML templates, CSS and JavaScript files are updated to ensure high-quality documentation.
-- API VIs and example are updated.
-- more details can be found in the user manual and at GitHub...

&lt;b&gt;VI Helpeks 3.0&lt;/b&gt;
-- &lt;u&gt;Free for Everyone&lt;/u&gt;:  The toolkit is now completely free to download and use. 
-- &lt;u&gt;Source-Available&lt;/u&gt;:  All VIs have unlocked Block Diagrams that allow for learning, modifying, and adapting the toolkit to fit any specific workflow.
-- &lt;u&gt;Dependency-Free Help&lt;/u&gt;:  This version eliminates third-party dependencies in its output by using new native JavaScript and CSS files instead of external libraries (e.g. jQuery). This enables the creation of high-quality HTML/CHM help while strengthening the security profile for both the toolkit itself and the help files it produces. This is especially important for aligning with new security standards, such as the EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA).
-- &lt;u&gt;Security&lt;/u&gt;:  To strengthen the toolkit's security profile in alignment with EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) principles, this version does not include any compiled binaries (EXE or DLL) and no longer automatically sets Windows file associations for its project files. File association can still be enabled on demand; see the "News and Changes" section in the VI Helpeks Help.
-- &lt;u&gt;General&lt;/u&gt;:  Includes various code optimizations and UI enhancements.
</Release_Notes>
    </Description>
